y I think that's okay? If they want the other card they'll say so. It saves a question.\n[00:03:56] Burcu Tan: Was that a real voice? The customer, I mean. It sounded like a real person.\n[00:04:00] Ozan Er: That's me [laughs]. I do the customers. And then I hung up there.\n[00:04:03] Burcu Tan: Very convincing.\n[00:04:05] Kerem Yalçın: Why did you hang up?\n[00:04:08] Ozan Er: Out of habit, the tests are long [laughs].\n[00:04:11] Kerem Yalçın: [laughs] Okay.\n[00:04:13] Selin Aydın: Wait, sorry, back to the cards. No. It should have asked about the other card there.\n[00:04:18] Deniz Arı: Before the offer, you mean?\n[00:04:19] Selin Aydın: Before. They called for the debt. If there is another card, first that. It says \"Başka bir kartınızın borcunu öğrenmek ister misiniz?\" and only when they say no, or there's no card left, then the offer.\n[00:04:31] Deniz Arı: Even if it's one more question?\n[00:04:33] Kerem Yalçın: Even then. Most people with two cards want both. And they don't know they can just say it, nobody knows what a bot can do.\n[00:04:40] Deniz Arı: Fair. Okay.\n[00:04:42] Ozan Er: And when they've heard all their cards...\n[00:04:44] Selin Aydın: Then the offer. And someone with one card, no question of course, that sounds silly.\n[00:04:49] Burcu Tan: Is that the same when the card had no debt? Sorry, I came in late on this.\n[00:04:53] Selin Aydın: The question, yes, if there's another card. What comes after it there, leave it as in my document.\n[00:04:57] Ozan Er: Okay. It was the order in our prompt, two parts fighting. I'll fix it.\n[00:05:01] Kerem Yalçın: And Ozan, back to the \"ge be pe\". Not \"Sterlin\". İngiliz Sterlini. We said it on Wednesday, Elçin was very clear.\n[00:05:07] Ozan Er: Ah, right, she was. Okay.\n[00:05:09] Kerem Yalçın: All four in full. No codes, no short forms.\n[00:05:12] Selin Aydın: So for that card it's... let me say it so you can copy it. \"Dolar ve İngiliz Sterlini borcunuz bulunmamaktadır.\"\n[00:05:20] Ozan Er: Typing.\n[00:05:21] Burcu Tan: And if the lira is the one with no debt, \"Türk Lirası borcunuz bulunmamaktadır\". I don't want to hear \"te le\" from a robot either.\n[00:05:27] Ozan Er: [typing] TL Türk Lirası, USD Dolar, EUR... Euro, GBP İngiliz Sterlini. Okay. The sentence won't see the code at all any more, only the names.\n[00:05:36] Deniz Arı: Sorry, I said shorter is nicer. Forget that.\n[00:05:39] Kerem Yalçın: [laughs] Forgotten.\n[00:05:41] Ozan Er: Call thirty-one. This is the strange one. The new card.\n[00:05:45] Selin Aydın: Which new card?\n[00:05:47] Ozan Er: In Mert's data there's one customer with a single card, the Yıldız Genç one, ending two zero two zero. No statement cut yet. In cards that balance the statement date and the due date are empty.\n[00:05:57] Selin Aydın: \"Cards that balance\"? [laughs]\n[00:05:59] Ozan Er: Cards dot balance. The service. Sorry, I'm tired.\n[00:06:02] Ozan Er: Listen. [plays recording, about ten seconds]\n[00:06:14] Kerem Yalçın: Fifth of October? Where does that come from?\n[00:06:17] Ozan Er: Nowhere. Not in the answer for that card. Many other test cards have the fifth of October, I think it copied that. The no-debt sentence has a date in it, \"... tarihli ekstresinden\", and the date was empty, so it filled the hole.\n[00:06:29] Kerem Yalçın: That's the worst thing it can do. Saying a date that doesn't exist.\n[00:06:33] Burcu Tan: Can't you just put the next statement date in that place? The service gives it, no?\n[00:06:38] Ozan Er: It gives the next statement date, yes. Fifth of November.\n[00:06:41] Burcu Tan: Then put that there and the sentence works.\n[00:06:44] Kerem Yalçın: No, then the sentence says there's a statement from the fifth of November. There isn't one. It's in the future.\n[00:06:49] Burcu Tan: Ah. True. Okay, no.\n[00:06:51] Selin Aydın: In September Kerem said no debt and don't invent a date. That's still the idea.\n[00:06:56] Ozan Er: What if it just says there's no debt because no statement has been cut yet, and then, if the answer has it, when the first one comes. Only that date, exactly as the service gives it. Nothing else.\n[00:07:07] Ozan Er: Something like \"Kartınızın henüz kesilmiş bir ekstresi olmadığı için ekstre borcunuz bulunmamaktadır. İlk hesap kesim tarihiniz 5 Kasım 2026 olacak.\" with the date from the answer.\n[00:07:17] Kerem Yalçın: Yeah, let's do that.\n[00:07:19] Selin Aydın: Mm.\n[00:07:20] Kerem Yalçın: And if there's no date in the answer either, it just says there's no debt. That's fine too. Just nothing made up.\n[00:07:25] Deniz Arı: Is somebody frying something?\n[00:07:27] Burcu Tan: [laughs] That's my kitchen. Muting.\n[00:07:30] Selin Aydın: Ozan, how many more? Kerem has to go.\n[00:07:33] Ozan Er: Not a call, a dry run. Deniz played the customer.\n[00:07:36] Deniz Arı: The cut day. We can't hit it with the test data, the dates are fixed, so I told the assistant today is the cut day and called.\n[00:07:44] Ozan Er: [plays recording, about fifteen seconds]\n[00:07:59] Burcu Tan: It started with the due date.\n[00:08:01] Ozan Er: Yes. \"Borçlarınız için son ödeme tarihiniz [son ödeme tarihi]'dir.\" first, then the amount.\n[00:08:07] Burcu Tan: In the IVR the first thing is that the statement is cut tonight. \"Hesap kesim tarihiniz bugün, ekstreniz saat 00.00 itibarıyla kesilecek.\" That's in Selin's document too, it's what the menu does today.\n[00:08:17] Deniz Arı: And then after that the normal reading, the statement debt, like any other day?\n[00:08:21] Kerem Yalçın: I don't mind how it opens, honestly.\n[00:08:23] Burcu Tan: I do, a bit. People hear the due date and think the bill is out.\n[00:08:27] Kerem Yalçın: Fine, then use yours. But the other one isn't wrong. What I care about is the number.\n[00:08:32] Selin Aydın: Which number did it read, Ozan?\n[00:08:34] Ozan Er: The statement debt. From the last statement.\n[00:08:37] Kerem Yalçın: That's the problem then. On the cut day the last statement is from a month ago. They need the total, with everything they spent since then in it.\n[00:08:44] Deniz Arı: Ah, so not what I said. Not the normal reading.\n[00:08:46] Kerem Yalçın: No. Opening whichever, then the total debt.\n[00:08:49] Ozan Er: The totalDebt field then, per currency. Mert's contract says it includes the spending after the statement.\n[00:08:55] Selin Aydın: Yes, that one.\n[00:08:57] Burcu Tan: I'd still put the 00.00 one first. It tells them why the number is bigger than the last bill.\n[00:09:02] Kerem Yalçın: Put it first. I just don't want the other one treated as wrong.\n[00:09:06] Burcu Tan: Okay, okay.\n[00:09:08] Ozan Er: And the currency names in the total too, full names. [laughs] Before Kerem says it.\n[00:09:12] Kerem Yalçın: [laughs] Good.\n[00:09:14] Kerem Yalçın: Guys, I need to drive. Anything else that needs me?\n[00:09:17] Deniz Arı: No, the rest is on our side. The voice speed on long amounts.\n[00:09:20] Kerem Yalçın: Okay. Bye all.\n[00:09:22] Burcu Tan: Bye Kerem, good game.\n[00:09:24] Selin Aydın: Bye.\n[00:09:26] Selin Aydın: Deniz, I won't get to the document this weekend. Can you send Elçin and Mert a few lines?\n[00:09:31] Deniz Arı: Yes, I'll write something short. Maybe Monday morning.\n[00:09:34] Selin Aydın: Monday is fine.\n[00:09:36] Ozan Er: Selin, the mobile app topic from Wednesday, is that still next week?\n[00:09:40] Selin Aydın: Next week, yes, Thursday I think. Kerem sends the invite.\n[00:09:44] Ozan Er: Okay.\n[00:09:45] Burcu Tan: Deniz, send me the recording link too? I want my team to hear the \"ge be pe\" [laughs].\n[00:09:50] Deniz Arı: [laughs] Sure.\n[00:09:52] Burcu Tan: Okay, kids are calling. Bye.\n[00:09:54] Selin Aydın: Bye. Thanks both, enjoy the weekend.\n[00:09:56] Deniz Arı: You too. Bye.\n\n[recording stopped]\n\n=== FILE: statement-debt-call-flow.pdf ===\nTL: not paid\ndebt and minimum\nReturn to supervisor\nCall arrives from IVR\nSupervisor detects intent\nhands off to statement debt assistant\nSecond factor\nneeded?\nyes\nBack to IVR for second factor\nthen return to the assistant\nno\nCard list service\nEligible\ncards?\nnone\nyes\nReturn to supervisor\nHow many?\nmore than 1\nName the customer's cards\nask which one\nSame card\nname?\nyes\nAsk last 4 digits\n1\nSame last\n4 digits?\nno\nyes\nyes\nAsk last 6 digits\nno\nCard selected\nStatement\ndebt?\nnone\nyes\nSay there is no statement debt\nread total debt\nRead last 4 digits, card name,\ncut-off and due date\nAnother\ncard?\nTL debt?\nno\nyes\nno\nReturn to supervisor\nTL payment\nstatus\nnone paid\nmin or more\nbelow min\nNo TL debt\nTL: minimum or more paid\nremaining debt, thanks\nTL: below minimum paid\ndebt, minimum, remaining\nUSD / EUR\ndebt?\nRead USD / EUR debt\nor say there is none\nRead due date\nOffer: change cut-off date\nor e-mail the statement\nCustomer\nanswer\nnothing else pay debt\ne-mail\ncut-off date\nIVR: transfer to agent\nRegistered\ne-mail?\nyes\nRead the registered address\nno\nSend to this\naddress?\nyes no\nSend statement by e-mail\nSay there is no suitable address\nReturn to supervisor\nShared\nstatement?\nyes\nno\nPrimary or\nlinked card?\nlinked\nprimary\nRead the card's cut-off week\nRead linked and primary card\ncut-off week and next dates\nRead primary and linked card\ncut-off week and next dates\nChange it?\nyes\nOffer the other weeks\ncustomer picks one\nno\nRead the new week and dates\nget confirmation\nReturn to supervisor\n\n=== FILE: test-environment/test-customers.json ===\n{\n  \"description\": \"Freya Bank voice test environment: synthetic customers (fictional, no real people or cards) and the exact response each statement service returns for them. Shapes follow the 2026-10-01 service contract. Under 'services', services called with a card are keyed by the masked card number from cards.list; statement.week.decide and statement.week.change have a second key, the requested week (newStatementWeek). 'http' is the status code, 'response' the response body